A||||4||Jason Kamrud||V8 fuel pump pressure...?||||1||
Z||000000||Jason Kamrud||08-14-2001||12:59 AM||||The stock 2.8 fuel pump puts out like 50 PSI, way too much for a quadrajunk.  Has anyone put a fuel pressure regulator on the fuel line? They sell for like 20 bucks & are adjustable from like 5 to 15 psi. Does the stock fuel pump put out too much pressure for one of these? Will it regulate that high of pressure down to like 8-10 lbs? I also heard of putting on a pump off of a TBI 4-cyl. car, but I would like to avoid that if possible b/c I'm sure they're pretty spendy. I could go with a mechanical pump, but I like electric ones-you don't have to pump it while cranking. I would like to hear what people are doing out there & what works and what doesn't.<P>------------------<BR>Jason Kamrud||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-14-2001||08:06 AM||||Everyone I've talked to use either a mechanical pump or a 2M4 fuel pump with a regulator. You may run into reliability problems trying to redue the pressure from 50 to 4-6 lbs. If you don't break the regulator you'll probably burn the pump up.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||cowans||08-14-2001||11:18 AM||||Jason, I'm running a SBC and used a 2M4 fuel pump with a adjustable regulator (approx 5.5 lbs), so far so good. Just make sure when you replace the pump to seat it properly in its rubber holder, otherwise you will get a headache with the cockpit noise....been there, done that!!!! taking out the tank twice was not fun!!!<BR>Sandy||||reg||1
Z||000003||cardealer||08-14-2001||12:15 PM||||i started with a fiero 4 cyl fuel pump from auto zone (35.00) it put out about 8 1/2 psi.<BR>i used a adjustable regulator to bring it down to 4 1/2. it worked great, however when i change may cam, heads, carb, and added n20 i added a holley "blue" fuel pump to run just the n20 and raised the fuel pressure to 6 psi on both lines. if your car came with a 6 cyl, you will need to drop the tank to swap out the fuel pumps but it is real easy to do.<BR>good luck!<BR>tony||||reg||1
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||08-14-2001||03:19 PM||||Carddealer is right.  The 4 cyl stock fuel pump has low enough psi that it can be regulated down without burning up the pump.  The 6 cyl pump eventually burns out.  It happened twice to my buddy until he learned about the 4 cyl pump.||||reg||1
